# TypeScript Standards

Source: [awesome-cursorrules/rules/typescript.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Types
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; use `type` for unions, intersections, and mapped types
- Never use `any`; use `unknown` and narrow with type guards
- Enable strict mode; use `readonly` for immutable config objects
- Suffix React prop interfaces with `Props` (e.g. `StatCardProps`)

## Naming
- PascalCase: components, interfaces, types
- camelCase: variables, functions, hooks
- UPPER_SNAKE_CASE: constants and env keys

## Functions
- Explicit return types on exported functions and hooks
- Prefer `async/await`; model expected failures as typed results or discriminated unions
- Custom error types for domain failures (e.g. `ContainmentApiError`)

## Organization
- Shared API types live in `frontend/lib/types.ts` aligned with backend Pydantic models
- Barrel exports only when they reduce noise; avoid deep re-export chains
- Co-locate small helper types with the component that owns them

## Patterns
- Use discriminated unions for verdict/severity states (`SAFE | SUSPICIOUS | BREACHED`)
- Type guards for runtime API responses before rendering live dashboard data
- Avoid type assertions; validate external JSON at the fetch boundary
